    fullDescription: "Two of the best excursions from Cancún are to the islands of Isla Mujeres and Cozumel, and both are reached by comfortable, modern passenger ferries. Isla Mujeres is the easy one: the fast Ultramar catamarans cross from the mainland in about 20 minutes, running roughly every half hour from early morning until late at night, so you can go over for the day (or evening) at will. The main departure point is Puerto Juárez / Gran Puerto, just north of downtown Cancún, which is the cheapest option (around $19–21 round trip); there are also more expensive but convenient departures from several Hotel Zone piers such as Playa Tortugas and Playa Caracol. Buy tickets at the terminal or online, keep the return portion safe, and note the last ferry time if you're staying for sunset. Cozumel, Mexico's premier diving island, takes more planning: there's no direct ferry from Cancún, so you first travel about an hour south to Playa del Carmen (easily done by ADO bus or car), then catch the ferry across the channel, a 45-minute crossing run frequently by two competing operators for around $25 round trip. Both islands reward the effort — Isla Mujeres for its gorgeous calm-water beaches and relaxed vibe, Cozumel for its world-class reefs. For Isla Mujeres, take the cheaper Puerto Juárez ferry and go early; for Cozumel, combine the bus and ferry or take an organised tour; and always check the last return sailing before you set out.",
