    fullDescription: "Cancún flight prices swing sharply with the seasons, and understanding the calendar can save a great deal. The cheapest time to fly is the autumn low season, roughly from late August through early December, excluding the Thanksgiving week — September and October in particular see the lowest fares (round-trips from the US can dip toward $260 or less), partly because this coincides with the rainiest, most hurricane-prone months. Prices then climb steeply for the winter high season from mid-December, peaking over the Christmas and New Year holidays when both fares and hotels hit their most expensive, and staying high through the North American spring-break period of February to April, when students flood the city. There's a second, smaller peak in the mid-summer months of July and August, driven by family and European holidays and Mexican domestic travel, though it's less extreme than the winter and spring peaks. For the best value, aim for the shoulder windows of late April to May or November, when the weather is still good but the crowds and prices have eased. Whenever you go, booking well in advance (particularly for the pricey holiday periods), flying midweek rather than at weekends, staying flexible with your dates and setting fare alerts all help secure a better deal. Cancún benefits from huge competition on US and Canadian routes, including many low-cost carriers, which keeps fares keen outside the peaks — so shop around, and avoid the Christmas and spring-break spikes if your budget matters most.",
